US DOJ and CFTC sue Arkansas to stop its enforcement action against Kalshi

The US Department of Justice and the CFTC filed suit on November 12 in federal court in the Eastern District of Arkansas against Attorney General Tim Griffin, who had sued Kalshi in state court eight days earlier. The agencies argue that the Commodity Exchange Act gives the CFTC exclusive authority over event contracts, so state gambling law cannot apply. The suit also seeks to block future state actions against CFTC-regulated prediction markets.

